<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1971" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄθετ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίθημι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without position</i> or <i>place</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μονὰς οὐσία ἄ., στιγμὴ δὲ οὐσία
					θετός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>AP</u>
					0.87a36
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1016b25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1084b27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>not in its place</i>, i.e. lying about, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλίνθος, λίθος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				1.322i10
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>not adopted</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Posidipp.
				39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anon.Rhythm.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				9iv16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>wasted, useless</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					18.9.10
				</span></i>
			; <i>unfit, to be rejected</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					11.15
				</span></i>
			: c. dat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥευματισμοῖς,
			σπληνικοῖς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.128
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.70.6
			</span></i>; of persons, <i>incompetent,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PAmh.
				2.64.12
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθέσμως</span>
			, <i>lawlessly, despotically</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				150
			</span></i> (lyr.); <i>unsuitably</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχειν πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.715b
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Philum.
				<u>Ven.</u>
				2.3
			</span></i>.</div>
